.TH RATTBUILD 1 "2026-10-05" "Rattpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rattbuild \- construct, execute, and export Rattscript build graphs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rattbuild
.RB [ build
.RI [ TARGET ...]]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattbuild graph
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattbuild export
.BI \--to= EXPORTER
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattbuild clean
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rattbuild \--init
.RB [ \--profile= NAME]
.RB [ \--scaffold ]
.RB [ \-C " DIRECTORY" ]
.br
.B rattbuild \--list-profiles
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rattbuild
loads the root Rattspec and automatically discovers subordinate
Rattspec.m files.
It evaluates Rattscript to construct a deterministic build DAG, then executes
its actions incrementally and in parallel or exports the graph to another build
system. Side effects during construction are rejected; action blocks run during
execution. Package dependencies must already have been fetched by
.BR rattpkg (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build [TARGET ...]
Build selected targets and their prerequisites, or all targets when no names
are supplied. This is the default command. Namespaces are part of target names,
for example core::codec. The whole spec tree is validated even for a selected
target. Prints executed work and built/up-to-date counts.
.TP
.B graph
Serialize the graph as JSON, or DOT with
.BR \--dot .
No build actions run. Output goes to standard output unless
.B \-o
is supplied. Preserve the embedded canonical payload in DOT files for lossless
reimport.
.TP
.B export
Export the complete frozen graph using the exporter selected by
.BR \--to .
Exporters consume the DAG without evaluating Rattscript again. The default
output directory is build/export/EXPORTER under the selected project.
Generated build files invoke the recorded Rattpack host to run frozen actions.
.TP
.B clean
Remove graph-declared generated files, the graph's build cache, and its local
\&.rattpack working directory. Cleaning applies to the whole graph and does not
remove cached packages.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " DIRECTORY" ", \--directory=" DIRECTORY
Select the project root containing Rattspec. Default: current directory.
This does not change the shell working directory: relative CLI paths for
\--import, \-o, and a plugin \--to are relative to the invoking directory.
Imported graphs retain their recorded root.
.TP
.BI \-j " N" ", \--jobs=" N
Maximum simultaneous actions. Default: 0, which consults build.jobs in the
configuration, then the logical CPU count. N must be nonnegative.
.TP
.B \--warnings-as-errors
Treat configuration and specification warnings as failures.
.TP
.B \--init
Create a root Rattspec using the selected initialization profile.
.TP
.BI \--profile= NAME
Choose an initialization profile. Default: empty. Shipped profiles are c-exe,
c-lib, cxx-exe, cxx-lib, d-exe, d-lib, monorepo, and empty.
.TP
.B \--scaffold
With \--init, also create the profile's buildable sources and package scaffold.
.TP
.B \--list-profiles
List available profiles and exit, including when combined with \--init.
Listing and initialization install missing shipped profiles in the user profile
directory.
.TP
.B \--dot
Use DOT output for graph. Takes precedence over \--json.
.TP
.B \--json
Request JSON graph output, which is the default.
.TP
.BI \--import= FILE
Read a saved JSON or DOT graph instead of loading specifications.
.TP
.BI \-o " PATH" ", \--output=" PATH
Write graph output to a file, or exporter output to a directory.
.TP
.BI \--to= EXPORTER
Select cmake, gnumake (alias make), ninja, meson, or a native exporter library
path. Use an explicit output directory when selecting a library path.
.TP
.B \--hermetic
Mark actions strict and enforce frozen input/tool identities and declared
execution access. Graph capture and export preserve these flags. Strict
subprocess execution requires a supported platform sandbox.
.TP
.B \--dry-run
Preview stale build actions without executing them or updating the cache.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \--version
Display the version and exit.
.PP
Boolean long options also accept the parser's negative spelling, such as
\--no-dry-run. Internal __run-action options are reserved for generated exporters.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Rattspec
Root specification with project identity and at least one target.
.TP
.I Rattspec.m
Automatically discovered subordinate specification; must declare module().
Nested independent projects must be declared as monorepo members, vendored
projects, or ignored paths in the root specification.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rattpack/Config.toml
Configuration environment. Defaults to ~/.config/rattpack/Config.toml on POSIX.
Config.yaml is accepted; TOML wins if both exist and emits W_DUAL_CONFIG.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rattpack/buildprof/*.in
User initialization profiles, preprocessed as Rattscript templates.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration and initialization profiles.
Windows uses the rattpack directory under APPDATA.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success, help, or version output; 1 indicates an application
diagnostic or failed action; 2 indicates argument parsing failure.
Diagnostics go to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rattbuild build app \-j 8
rattbuild \--init \--profile=cxx-exe \--scaffold
rattbuild graph \--dot \-o graph.dot
rattbuild build \--import graph.dot
rattbuild export \--to=ninja \-o generated/ninja
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rattpkg (1),
.BR rattsc (1),
.BR rattspec (1),
.BR ratt-language-server (1)
.PP
The Rattpack manual is installed under share/rattpack/manual in the prefix.
